\documentclass{article}
\title{Interface Engineering for Solid-State Electrolytes}
\author{Li Wei}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Methods}
We synthesized the electrolyte powder by ball milling. The powder is pressed into pellets at 300 MPa. We coated the interface with a thin buffer layer. Symmetric cells are assembled in an argon glovebox. We measured the impedance every hour for 24 hours. The critical current density is determined by stepping the applied current.
\section{Results}
The buffer layer reduces interfacial resistance and suppresses dendrite growth.
\end{document}
